{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyFzRS3Gjhmt9TbPvhbt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Plan to Wire `check:pricing-sync` into Pre-Commit Hook\n\n1. **Check if a pre-commit hook already exists**\n   - Look for `.git/hooks/pre-commit` file\n   - If it exists, read it to understand the current hook structure\n\n2. **Verify the check command works**\n   - Run `npm run check:pricing-sync` locally to confirm it exits 0 on success and non-zero on mismatch\n   - Confirm it completes in ~2 seconds as expected\n\n3. **Identify the hook setup mechanism**\n   - Check for Husky config (`.husky/` directory, `husky` in `package.json`)\n   - Check for other hook tooling (`.githooks/`, manual scripts directory, etc.)\n   - Check `package.json` for any existing pre-commit hook configuration\n\n4. **Add the check to the pre-commit hook**\n   - If using Husky: add/edit `.husky/pre-commit` to include `npm run check:pricing-sync`\n   - If manual: directly edit `.git/hooks/pre-commit` (or create it with appropriate exit behavior)\n   - Ensure the hook fails (exits non-zero) if the check fails, preventing commit\n\n5. **Make the hook executable**\n   - Run `chmod +x .husky/pre-commit` (or equivalent for your hook mechanism)\n\n6. **Test the hook**\n   - Deliberately introduce a mismatch between the two files\n   - Attempt to commit and verify the hook blocks it\n   - Revert the mismatch and verify commit succeeds\n\n7. **Verify hook persists for the team**\n   - Confirm hook files are tracked in version control (not in `.gitignore`)\n   - Document in README or team docs if this is non-obvious"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":420,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
